	You didn't mention one of the advantages of the Priest and Samurai. 
Both classes start out with the "super-kick".  This means that they are
never injured by kicking chests, and can kick to hit more often and do
more damage.  At low levels, the Priest's kick is a lot better than his
weapons.
	I've played more Tourists than any other class(I like a chalange.), and
I've discovered that using the camera is normally a bad move because a
stunned monster is often more random and therefore more danagerous than
a normal monster.  A Tourist should not read his scrolls of magic
mapping either, because then he'll go down the first few levels too
quickly and be killed.  Your advantage is that you have a lot of food,
so time is on your side.  Play very cautiously.  Take advantage of your
pet.  Take advantage of altars.  Don't drink your potions of extra
healing until you're down a few hits (not too many, though -- you want
the permanant hits)  If you start with tins of spinach, that helps a
lot.  These days, I play knights, because I've decided that they're even
lamer than tourists.
	No matter what class you are, the most crucial resistance to get is
poison.  That's why barbarians are the best class.

